# What Vercel must never upload.
#
# The CLI uploads the whole project directory, not just what the build needs.
# Without this it tries to send src-tauri/target — 5.7GB of Rust build
# artifacts — and dies with "Upload aborted" long before it reaches the site.

# Rust build output. Regenerated by cargo, useless to a web deploy.
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/

# Installed on Vercel's side from the lockfile.
node_modules/

# Signed installers. These belong on GitHub Releases; a 64MB binary in a static
# deploy is both slow and the wrong place for it.
public/downloads/

# Local build output. Vercel runs its own build.
dist/

# Credentials, in case an ignore rule is ever loosened elsewhere.
.env
.env.*
supabase/.env.functions

.git/
